 html←PrepareHtmlPageForMajorVersionList(packageID data);majors;group;name;newestID;description;noOfMajors
⍝ Not indexed: this page is a list of links and has no content of its own, nor any prospect
⍝ of any. A crawler is still welcome to follow the links out of it - "noindex" alone leaves
⍝ "follow" at its default - and a visitor sees no difference.
⍝ `data` comes from `ListMajorVersions`: [;1] group and name, [;2] major version number,
⍝ [;3] number of releases.
⍝ The newest major version comes first. They are sorted by number here because the folder
⍝ names they come from sort as text, which would put 9 behind 15.
⍝ The description is the one of the newest release of the newest major version.
 majors←{⊃2⊃⎕VFI ⍵}¨data[;2]
 data←data[⍒majors;]
 noOfMajors←≢data
 (group name)←2↑'-'(≠⊆⊢)packageID
 newestID←⊃⌽Reg.ListVersions G.RegistryPath,packageID,'-',⊃data[1;2]   ⍝ Tatin's order: the best comes last
 description←GetPackageDescription G.RegistryPath,newestID
 html←(1 packageID '/packages')HtmlHeader''
 html,←⊂'<div class="page-head">'
 html,←⊂GetBreadcrumb('Packages'(Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/packages'))(group(GetGroupHref group))(name'')
 html,←⊂'<h2>',(EscapeSpecialChars name),' <span class="page-sub">',(⍕noOfMajors),' major version',((1≠noOfMajors)/'s'),'</span></h2>'
 :If 0<≢description
     html,←⊂'<p class="lead">',(EscapeSpecialChars description),'</p>'
 :EndIf
 html,←⊂'</div>'
 html,←⊂'<div class="major-list">'
 html,←(1=⍳noOfMajors)PrepareHtmlPageForMajorVersionList_¨↓data
 html,←⊂'</div>'
 html,←⊆GetFooter
 html,←⊂'</body>'
 html,←⊂'</html>'
⍝Done
